# Facility-attribution intermediates. The chain is
#   update_final_facility_classification.R      -> _final_v2
#   integrate_cpt_claims_into_facility_...R     -> _final_v3
#   analyze_open_payments_clinical_depth.R      -> _final_v4
# v2 and v3 are strict COLUMN SUBSETS of v4 and exist only to be read by the
# next stage, so 16 MB of near-duplicate person-level rows were tracked to
# record a state that the head of the chain already contains. Regenerate by
# running the producers in order. _final_v4 stays tracked, as do
# _attributions_complete and _hospital_rigorous_attributions, which carry 22
# and 36 columns that v4 does not.
artifacts/cohort_midwife_facility_attributions_final_v2.csv
artifacts/cohort_midwife_facility_attributions_final_v3.csv

# =============================================================================
# Person-level outputs of the attribute layers (identity + address + phone)
# =============================================================================
# README states that person-level rows are gitignored and rebuildable. These
# rules make that true for the layers added in the organization-linkage,
# Medicare, HCRIS and Open Payments work. Each file below carries
# certification_number and/or npi joined to a street address, a phone number,
# or an employer -- the AMCB-to-NPI pairing the repository already refuses to
# commit for artifacts/amcb_npi_linkage_FROZEN.csv.
#
# Every one is REBUILDABLE by running its producer; nothing here is a source.
# Aggregates stay tracked deliberately: table1_midwives.csv (111 rows, no
# person), hcris_affiliated_hospitals_fy2023.csv (902 facilities),
# org_resolution_ppv.csv, org_resolution_distribution_shift.csv.

