# the producer once someone has started filling human_verdict.
artifacts/org_resolution_review_sample.csv

# =============================================================================
# Tier 1a: named individuals joined to a DATE OF BIRTH
# =============================================================================
# voter_dob is a full date of birth taken from state voter files and joined to
# a named clinician. It was never published by AMCB, CMS or any licensure
# board -- the linkage is this project's own creation, and it is the most
# sensitive thing the repository has ever held.
#
# NOT REGENERABLE FROM ANYTHING LOCAL. match_ohio_voter_ages.R scrapes the Ohio
# Secretary of State portal live; no voter file exists on disk. Untracking is
# safe, LOSING THE LOCAL COPY IS NOT. Keep these in an access-controlled
# directory outside the repository and record a checksum, rather than deleting
# them.
#
# Nothing downstream breaks: the only consumers are
# calibrate_amcb_certification_ages.R and each file's own producer, and the
# reduced output they feed is artifacts/amcb_calibrated_ages.csv, 22,309 rows of
# certification_number + final_age with no DOB and no names.
#
# UPDATED 2026-08-14: that file was untracked too. This block used to say it
# "stays tracked", which was true when the voter files went and is not true now
# -- a certification number is the AMCB directory's own primary key, so 22,309
# of them plus an age is still a row per identifiable person.
artifacts/ohio_voter_license_ages.csv
artifacts/florida_voter_license_ages.csv
artifacts/**/*voter*ages*.csv
artifacts/**/*_dob*.csv

# =============================================================================
# Guard: frozen person-level copies must not bypass protection by filename
# =============================================================================
# `artifacts/amcb_npi_linkage_FROZEN.csv` is an EXACT path, so a date suffix or
# a subdirectory walks straight past it. Four copies of the 22,309-row
# AMCB-to-NPI pairing are tracked today under other names
# (amcb_npi_linkage_FROZEN_2026-08-08.csv,
# prelinkage_backup_20260810/amcb_npi_linkage_FROZEN.csv,
# frozen_stage2/midwives_with_nppes.csv, frozen_cohort/analytic_cohort.csv).
# All four are untracked as of 2026-08-14. Note that analytic_cohort.csv was
# never a copy of the pairing: 16,892 rows, certification_number only, no NPI
# and no name. It is untracked on the certification-number rule, not this one.
#
# THIS GLOB IS PREVENTIVE ONLY. .gitignore does not affect files already in the
# index, so the four existing copies REMAIN TRACKED until someone untracks them
# deliberately. This stops the NEXT one from being added by accident.
artifacts/**/amcb_npi_linkage_FROZEN*.csv
artifacts/**/*FROZEN*.csv

# =============================================================================
# The roster itself: name + certification number, one row per certificant
# =============================================================================
# Untracked 2026-08-14, acting on the note above -- these are the copies that
# "REMAIN TRACKED until someone untracks them deliberately".
#
# Ten files, 65 MB, each carrying last_name + first_name + certification_number
# for all 22,309 certificants, nine of them with the matched NPI beside it. That
# combination is the linkage this project exists to produce, and publishing it
# hands over the answer for every person in the roster at once.
#
# Every one is REBUILDABLE, which is why untracking is safe:
#   midwives.csv                  scrape.py
#   midwives_with_nppes.csv       match_nppes.R
#   midwives_geocoded.csv         geocode_midwives.R
#   midwives_status_check.csv     check_npi_deactivation.R
#   amcb_npi_linkage_FROZEN*.csv  reconcile_linkage.R
#   amcb_npi_crosswalk_*panel*    match_amcb_to_npi.R
#
# LOSING THE LOCAL COPY IS NOT SAFE, and a rebuild is not free -- the crosswalks
# are the output of a multi-hour matcher run. Keep them outside the repository
# and record a checksum rather than deleting them.
#
# These are still in git HISTORY. Untracking stops future commits; it does not
# unpublish what every existing clone already has. Purging that needs a history
# rewrite, which is a separate decision.
#
# Both artifacts/amcb_calibrated_ages.csv and
# artifacts/frozen_cohort/analytic_cohort.csv were held back at this step and
# untracked on 2026-08-14 with the rest of the baseline.
midwives.csv
midwives_geocoded.csv
midwives_status_check.csv
midwives_with_nppes.csv
artifacts/**/midwives_with_nppes.csv
artifacts/amcb_npi_crosswalk_*panel-midwifery-plus-nursing*.csv

